  "notes": "Clean integration worktree for semantic extraction from four historical ext4 worktrees. A1 is complete: only the current single-transaction JournalRing, PreparedJournalTransaction, and MutationHandle ownership path was extended to cover zero or more revoke pages. A2 release and allocation extraction is complete for current inline initialized extent plans, including cross-group bitmap/GDT merging, no-home-write rejection, and a Docker e2fsck fixture. A3 now covers depth-0 through bounded depth-3 unwritten conversion, including leaf split, root growth, full-parent carry, full depth-two root promotion into a depth-three inode root, and checked non-overflowing depth-three leaf conversion. The deep planner now also splits a full depth-three leaf and carries through full ancestors using immutable metadata-only claims. Bounded recursive truncate/destroy release is now wired through public format planners: it validates child/key ordering, cycles, reserved aliases, and physical overlap; emits descendant-first extent-node after-images; reserves readable journal trees; and carries sorted revoke/deferred-free claims. Docker debugfs now generates real Linux depth-two and ignored depth-three fragmented trees, and A6 runtime exchange is host-verified. The Tier 1 Docker runner live preflight is green, but no 1000-cut campaign or candidate receipt exists. M1/M2 high-DTB mapping and named role transport are complete. Real RV64 loader and cargo-metadata witnesses pass over TEST/SCRATCH/WORKLOAD, while a default-kernel frozen build remains CPU-bound after rustc startup and timed out at 1,800,000 ms without TX_GUEST_RUST_BUILD status=0. The sequential shell-test early-exit/reap fix, absolute-manifest runner path, BusyBox shell portability, and exported TEST wrapper environment are now recorded in the rustc materialization research note. M1/M2, M3, A6 crash acceptance, xfstests, and candidate Tier 1 receipt remain open. `cargo xtask progress validate` remains blocked by the unrelated missing SMP research reference."
